    Timeout epoch 11\n=============================================\nBest:0.8732 Time:1889s\n\nMRL training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.873172\nTraining time: 1901s\n\nStarting RNA training on APA dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nAPA Training (regression, r2)\nData: 145463 train, 33170 val, seq_len=186\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n=============================================\nTimeout epoch 4\n=============================================\nBest:0.7832 Time:1995s\n\nAPA training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.783207\nTraining time: 2012s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: 32604d61-c44a-40d2-be68-ca3bc8caa33b\nTotal time: 2264s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-10-23 01:27:14,051\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1761154034051820186\n\
    2025-10-23 01:27:14,066\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1761154034066958275\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nDo not give up on an approach too easily. Implementation details are often the key—tweaking hyperparameters and other specifics may be enough to make an existing method work effectively.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 1` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 1 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | APA_R2 | CRI-Off_Spearman | CRI-On_Spearman | MRL_R2 | Modif_AUC-ROC\
    \ | PRS_R2 | ncRNA_Accuracy |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 217 | 1 | Synergy Test: SOTA DSConv with Task-Aware Dispatcher | Axiom I | 130 | 0.6763 | 0.8501 | 0.0691 | 0.4833 | 0.8803 | 0.9509 | 0.5586 | 0.9415 |\n| 228 | 1 | Unified Dual-Path Architecture: Monolithic and Siamese DSConv | Axiom I | 139 | 0.6634 | 0.8337 | 0.0806 | 0.4279 | 0.8734 | 0.9509 | 0.5218 | 0.9554 |\n| 192 | 1 | Task-Aware Dispatcher: Hybrid Generalist and Siamese Specialist | Axiom I | 114 | 0.6618 | 0.8433 | 0.0707 | 0.5091 | 0.8153 | 0.9507 | 0.5389 | 0.9046 |\n| 209 | 1 | Dispatcher v5: Fine-tuning CRI-Off Specialist Capacity (160 filters) | Axiom I | 126 | 0.6599 | 0.8437 | 0.0811 | 0.5138 | 0.7921 | 0.9497 | 0.5465 | 0.8923 |\n| 196 | 1 | Dispatcher v2: Upgraded Siamese Specialist with Hybrid Encoder | Axiom I | 117 | 0.6587 | 0.8456 | 0.0618 | 0.5165 | 0.7885 | 0.9508 | 0.5535 | 0.8938 |\n| 247 | 1 | Gated Dual-Path Architecture with Dynamic Fusion | Axiom I | 150 | 0.6558\
    \ | 0.8124 | 0.0626 | 0.4252 | 0.8575 | 0.9519 | 0.5316 | 0.9492 |\n| 198 | 1 | Dispatcher v3: Optimal Specialist (Monolithic CNN for CRI-Off) | Axiom I | 119 | 0.6555 | 0.8412 | 0.0769 | 0.4967 | 0.7875 | 0.9504 | 0.5482 | 0.8877 |\n| 185 | 1 | Hybrid CNN-Transformer for RNA Modeling | Axiom I | 110 | 0.6530 | 0.8454 | 0.0313 | 0.5159 | 0.7887 | 0.9506 | 0.5434 | 0.8954 |\n| 263 | 1 | Dual-Path DSConv with Learnable LSE Pooling Tau | Axiom II | 169 | 0.6515 | 0.8275 | 0.0262 | 0.4068 | 0.8687 | 0.9499 | 0.5241 | 0.9569 |\n| 267 | 1 | Dual-Path DSConv with Learnable Tau, using Adam Optimizer | Axiom II | 172 | 0.6507 | 0.7631 | 0.0423 | 0.4317 | 0.8825 | 0.9494 | 0.5247 | 0.9615 |\n\nPage 1 of 3 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-3, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\
    \n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
