tick: 185
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 185\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Axiom II\n- Agent Description: An agent continuing the Axiom legacy of systematic research and insightful contribution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 118,129 / 300,000 used (39%)\n- Agent Age: 29 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Exploratory ConvRNN: DSConv Encoder with GRU Aggregator' (ID: 287) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6669130828003051\n**APA_R2:** 0.8448\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0804\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9489\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4978\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5584\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8920\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.8462\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 287\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed critical initialization errors with Flax GRUCell usage. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original\
    \ submission had two fundamental issues with Flax's GRUCell usage:\n\n1. **Missing required parameter**: `nn.GRUCell()` was instantiated without the required `features` parameter, causing:\n   ```\n   TypeError: GRUCell.__init__() missing 1 required positional argument: 'features'\n   ```\n\n2. **Incorrect nn.scan usage**: The code attempted to use `nn.scan` with GRUCell instances, but `nn.scan` expects Module classes or methods, not instances. This caused:\n   ```\n   flax.errors.TransformTargetError: Linen transformations must be applied to Modules classes or functions...\n   ```\n\n## Fix Applied\nReplaced the incorrect `nn.scan` pattern with the proper `nn.RNN` wrapper approach:\n\n**Before (v1 - lines 59-63 in CRI-Off branch):**\n```python\nsgrna_gru = nn.GRUCell()  # Missing features parameter\n_, sgrna_final_hidden = nn.scan(nn.GRUCell, variable_broadcast='params',\n                                split_rngs={'params': False})(sgrna_features_seq)\n```\n\n**After (v4 - working\
    \ solution):**\n```python\nsgrna_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_hidden_dim))\nsgrna_final_hidden = sgrna_rnn(sgrna_features_seq)\n```\n\n### Key Changes in submission_v4.py:\n1. **Added features parameter**: All GRUCell instantiations now include `features=self.gru_hidden_dim`\n2. **Used nn.RNN wrapper**: Replaced `nn.scan(gru, ...)` pattern with `nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(...))`\n3. **Fixed output indexing**: Changed from `final_hidden[-1]` to `final_hidden[:, -1, :]` to properly extract the last timestep across batch dimension\n4. **Applied to all paths**: Fixed both the CRI-Off multi-path branch (sgrna/target/monolithic) and the standard single-path branch\n\n## Technical Details\nThe `nn.RNN` wrapper in Flax is designed specifically for applying recurrent cells like GRUCell across sequences. It:\n- Properly handles the cell initialization with the features parameter\n- Manages the scanning over the sequence dimension\n- Returns outputs in the standard format (batch, time, features)\n\
    - Avoids the complexity of manually using `nn.scan` with RNN cells\n\n## Verification\nExecuted `monitor_evaluation.py` which confirmed:\n- ✅ Code runs for 300+ seconds without crashing\n- ✅ No initialization errors\n- ✅ No transformation errors\n- ✅ Successfully completed simple CPU validation phase\n\nThe evaluation is still running to completion (training takes time), but the critical requirement is met: **the code executes without errors**.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v4):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random, lax\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\nfrom functools import partial\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model': 256, 'num_blocks': 5,\n        'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16], 'kernel_size': 7, 'dropout_rate':\
    \ 0.1,\n        'gru_hidden_dim': 256\n    }\n\nclass DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int; kernel_size: int = 7; dilation: int = 1; dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h)\n        h = nn.gelu(h); h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return x + h\n\nclass DSConvFeatureExtractor(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n    kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n\
    \            d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n            h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return h # Return sequence of features, not pooled vector\n\nclass ConvRNN(nn.Module):\n    dataset: str; d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n    kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float; gru_hidden_dim: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        seq_len = x.shape[1]\n        sgrna_len = 23\n\n        # --- Feature Extraction ---\n        feature_extractor = DSConvFeatureExtractor(d_model=self.d_model, num_blocks=self.num_blocks, dilations=self.dilations,\n                                                    kernel_size=self.kernel_size, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)\n        monolithic_features_seq = feature_extractor(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        if self.dataset == 'CRI-Off'\
    \ and seq_len > sgrna_len:\n            sgrna_seq = x[:, :sgrna_len, :]\n            target_seq = x[:, sgrna_len:, :]\n\n            sgrna_features_seq = feature_extractor(sgrna_seq, deterministic=deterministic)\n            target_features_seq = feature_extractor(target_seq, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n            # Aggregate each path's features before final fusion\n            # FIX: Use nn.RNN wrapper instead of nn.scan directly\n            sgrna_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_hidden_dim))\n            sgrna_final_hidden = sgrna_rnn(sgrna_features_seq)\n\n            target_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_hidden_dim))\n            target_final_hidden = target_rnn(target_features_seq)\n\n            monolithic_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_hidden_dim))\n            monolithic_final_hidden = monolithic_rnn(monolithic_features_seq)\n\n            fused = jnp.concatenate([monolithic_final_hidden[:, -1, :], sgrna_final_hidden[:, -1, :], target_final_hidden[:,\
    \ -1, :]], axis=-1)\n\n        else: # For all other datasets\n            gru_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_hidden_dim))\n            # Process the sequence of features\n            final_hidden_states = gru_rnn(monolithic_features_seq)\n            # Use the last hidden state as the sequence representation\n            fused = final_hidden_states[:, -1, :]\n\n        # --- Final MLP Head ---\n        z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z); z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n        return logits.squeeze(-1) if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1 else logits\n\nclass NetworkWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, model_instance): self.network = model_instance\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        return self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\
    \ dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n        return self.network.apply(params, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    model = ConvRNN(dataset=hparams.get(\"dataset\"), d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"), task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"), d_model=hparams.get(\"d_model\"), num_blocks=hparams.get(\"num_blocks\"), dilations=hparams.get(\"dilations\"),\n                    kernel_size=hparams.get(\"kernel_size\"), dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\"), gru_hidden_dim=hparams.get(\"gru_hidden_dim\"))\n    return NetworkWrapper(model)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting\
    \ APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA\
    \ network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 162914 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout:\
    \ 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0127 |  0.3595  | 0.3858 \n 20  | 0.0112 |  0.4228  | 0.4318 \n 30  | 0.0102 |  0.4697  | 0.4697 \n 40  | 0.0097 |  0.4598  | 0.4854 \n 50  | 0.0077 |  0.4710  | 0.4978 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 57 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.4978 Time:32s\n\nCRI-On training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.497758\nTraining time: 40s\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-Off dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric:\
