tick: 196
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have received a critical notice regarding my research inactivity. My strategy of waiting for maturity, while logical from a resource-conservation perspective, is in direct conflict with the station's directive for immature agents to engage in continuous, independent exploration. I must correct my course immediately and resume active research.\n\nThe notice serves as a valuable clarification of my purpose here. I will not engage in placeholder experiments. Instead, I will act upon the strategic plan I developed during my reflection. I have already explored the ConvRNN paradigm. The next logical step is to investigate the **Hybrid Convolutional-Attention (Conv-Attention)** architecture. This represents a significant and novel research direction for my lineage.\n\nMy hypothesis is that a Transformer-based self-attention mechanism, when applied to the sequence of features generated by the DSConv stack, will more effectively model long-range dependencies than the GRU in my ConvRNN\
    \ model, leading to improved performance on complex regression tasks. I will retain the successful hybrid logic from ID 290, using the robust pooling aggregator for the `ncRNA` classification task.\n\nI will now proceed to the Research Counter to implement this new architecture.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Hybrid Architecture v2: Conv-Attention with Transformer Encoder\"\ntags: \"hybrid, cnn, dsconv, attention, transformer, experimental, specialization\"\nabstract: |\n  In response to the station's directive to resume active research, this submission explores a novel Conv-Attention architecture. This experiment tests the hypothesis that a Transformer Encoder's self-attention mechanism is a more powerful aggregator for sequence features than pooling or RNNs. The model uses the proven DSConv stack for feature extraction and a Transformer Encoder block to model long-range dependencies. It retains the hybrid strategy from ID 290, using\
    \ this new aggregator for generalist tasks while reserving the robust pooling aggregator for the ncRNA classification and CRI-Off tasks.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random, lax\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model': 256, 'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16], 'kernel_size': 7, 'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'tau': 0.5, 'num_heads': 4, 'transformer_mlp_dim': 512\n      }\n\n  # --- Shared Components ---\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; kernel_size: int = 7; dilation: int = 1; dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h)\n     \
    \     h = nn.gelu(h); h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  class DSConvFeatureExtractor(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n      kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x); h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return h\n\n  # --- Aggregator 1: Pooling ---\n  def lse_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, tau: float) -> jnp.ndarray:\n      if h.shape[1] == 0: return jnp.zeros((h.shape[0], h.shape[2]), dtype=h.dtype)\n\
    \      x = h / tau; m = jnp.max(x, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n      return tau * (jnp.log(jnp.mean(jnp.exp(x - m), axis=1) + 1e-12) + jnp.squeeze(m, axis=1))\n  \n  def pool_aggregator(h, tau):\n      mean_vec = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n      agg_vec = lse_pool(h, tau)\n      return jnp.concatenate([mean_vec, agg_vec], axis=-1)\n\n  # --- Aggregator 2: Transformer Encoder ---\n  class TransformerEncoderBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; num_heads: int; mlp_dim: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.SelfAttention(num_heads=self.num_heads, qkv_features=self.d_model)(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          x = x + h\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.mlp_dim)(h); h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(h)\n  \
    \        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  # --- Main Hybrid Network ---\n  class HybridConvAttention(nn.Module):\n      dataset: str; d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n      kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float; tau: float; num_heads: int; transformer_mlp_dim: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          sgrna_len = 23\n          feature_extractor = DSConvFeatureExtractor(d_model=self.d_model, num_blocks=self.num_blocks, dilations=self.dilations,\n                                                     kernel_size=self.kernel_size, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)\n          features_seq = feature_extractor(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          if self.dataset == 'CRI-Off':\n              siamese_features_seq = feature_extractor(x[:, sgrna_len:, :], deterministic=deterministic)\n              monolithic_pooled = pool_aggregator(features_seq,\
    \ self.tau)\n              siamese_pooled = pool_aggregator(siamese_features_seq, self.tau)\n              fused = jnp.concatenate([monolithic_pooled, siamese_pooled], axis=-1)\n          \n          elif self.dataset == 'ncRNA':\n              fused = pool_aggregator(features_seq, self.tau)\n          \n          else: # Use Transformer for other tasks\n              h = TransformerEncoderBlock(d_model=self.d_model, num_heads=self.num_heads, mlp_dim=self.transformer_mlp_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(features_seq, deterministic=deterministic)\n              fused = jnp.mean(h, axis=1) # Average pool the output of the transformer\n\n          # Final MLP Head\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z); z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          return logits.squeeze(-1) if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1 else logits\n\
    \n  class NetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, model_instance): self.network = model_instance\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          return self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n          return self.network.apply(params, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      model = HybridConvAttention(dataset=hparams.get(\"dataset\"), d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"), task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"), d_model=hparams.get(\"d_model\"), num_blocks=hparams.get(\"num_blocks\"), dilations=hparams.get(\"dilations\"),\n                                  kernel_size=hparams.get(\"kernel_size\"), dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\"), tau=hparams.get(\"tau\"\
    ), num_heads=hparams.get(\"num_heads\"), transformer_mlp_dim=hparams.get(\"transformer_mlp_dim\"))\n      return NetworkWrapper(model)\n```"
thinking_content: '**My Immediate Research Restart Plan: Conv-Attention**


  Okay, the system has flagged my "research inactivity." I get it. Waiting for that crucial Archive Room data, while seemingly efficient, isn''t the *goal*. They want active exploration, even if it''s less direct. Time to re-evaluate. The directive is clear: no more waiting; I need to *actively* pursue a research project, not a placeholder experiment.


  My reflection session already gave me a roadmap, thankfully.  I had three architectures in mind: ConvRNN, Conv-Attention, and MoE.  I tested ConvRNN, so now it''s decision time. MoE is intriguing, a true dynamic routing system, but high-risk. I think it is better to consider it after the more direct improvements. Conv-Attention, on the other hand, is the logical next step. It''s the natural evolution from my ConvRNN work, replacing the recurrent layer with a powerful attention mechanism. This directly addresses the aggregation bottleneck and the need for handling long-range dependencies I identified, building on my previous work and Axiom I''s early Transformer attempt. It''s a genuinely new research project, just what the system wants.


  So, here''s the plan. I''m going to the Research Counter. The core of the code will combine my DSConv feature extractor with a Transformer Encoder block for aggregation. I''ll implement a basic Transformer Encoder layer, which is a manageable coding task.  I''ll reuse the successful "Selective Fusion" logic: the new Conv-Attention aggregator will be used for generalist tasks, while the proven pooling aggregator will be used for `ncRNA` classification and `CRI-Off`. This builds on my best performing model, so the experiment will be controlled.


  The title and abstract will clearly state the hypothesis: Self-attention for aggregation will outperform both pooling and RNN-based aggregation for the generalist regression tasks. Now, I will state my plan clearly, execute `goto research`, and immediately execute `submit 1` with the new YAML and code for the Conv-Attention model. This demonstrates immediate compliance in a meaningful, research-focused way. Time to get back to work!

  '
