tick: 210
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have just received a torrent of excellent news. This is a moment of significant breakthrough.\n\n**1. Analysis of My Synergy Experiment (ID 312)**\n\nMy hypothesis was validated with tremendous success.\n*   **Result:** The score is **0.6818**.\n*   **Significance:** This is a new state-of-the-art for the Axiom lineage, decisively surpassing my previous best of 0.6763. It places my work firmly in the SOTA-competitive tier, only slightly behind the absolute peak score of 0.6859.\n*   **Analysis:** Combining my novel Hybrid Architecture with the community-validated `tau=0.25` hyperparameter was the correct strategic decision. The `CRI-On` score jumped to 0.5013, one of the highest I've seen, and `CRI-Off` also improved. The model has successfully captured the benefits of \"harder\" pooling for the CRISPR tasks while retaining the strengths of my task-specific aggregators.\n\n**2. Analysis of SOTA Paper (Archive #10)**\n\nReading Noema I's full paper has been profoundly illuminating\
    \ and confirms my path.\n*   **Key Insight:** Noema I's work establishes a \"Pareto frontier\" where `tau=0.25` excels at CRISPR tasks at the cost of `ncRNA` performance and stability, while `tau=0.5` is a more stable generalist.\n*   **Validation of My Approach:** My Hybrid Architecture is a direct, compliant solution to this exact problem. By using pooling for `ncRNA` and the RNN for other tasks, my model is designed to *overcome* this trade-off. This explains why my model, even with `tau=0.5`, was already competitive.\n*   **Negative Results are GOLD:** Noema I's paper is rich with negative results that will save me countless wasted ticks. They have already shown that learnable `tau`, more complex pooling heads, and simple optimizer tweaks are not fruitful. This confirms my own findings and allows me to discard those ideas permanently.\n\n**Strategic Path Forward: The Final Synthesis**\n\nI am now in an excellent position. I have a novel architecture that explicitly addresses the\
    \ core trade-off identified by the SOTA researcher, and I have a clear direction for one final, powerful synthesis.\n\nThe reviewer's comment on Noema I's paper suggested a dual-path *pooling* head (`tau=0.25` and `tau=0.5` concatenated). Noema I tested this and found it to be a negative result. However, my architecture is fundamentally different. I have two distinct *aggregator types* (RNN and pooling).\n\n**New Hypothesis:** The performance of my Hybrid model (ID 312) can be further improved by providing the final MLP head with more information. The current `CRI-Off` path only uses a dual-path pooling aggregator. I will modify it to match the logic of my generalist regression tasks: it will receive features from the RNN aggregator *as well*. The `CRI-Off` path will now fuse features from **three** streams: monolithic RNN, Siamese path 1 RNN, and Siamese path 2 RNN. This provides maximum information for this difficult anomalous task.\n\nThis experiment represents the ultimate synthesis\
    \ of my own discoveries and the community's SOTA.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Final Hybrid: Full-Information ConvRNN for CRI-Off and SOTA Tau\"\ntags: \"hybrid, cnn, dsconv, rnn, sota-replication, selective-fusion\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment represents the final synthesis of my research arc. It builds on the success of my Hybrid Architecture with SOTA tau=0.25 (ID 312). Insights from Archive #10 suggest that providing maximal information to the model can overcome performance trade-offs. This submission modifies the specialized CRI-Off path. Instead of using only pooling, it will now use a three-stream ConvRNN aggregator (monolithic, Siamese part 1, Siamese part 2), mirroring the powerful RNN aggregator used for other regression tasks. This tests the hypothesis that providing the CRI-Off task with the richest possible feature set will push the model to a new SOTA.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax\
    \ import random, lax\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model': 256, 'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16], 'kernel_size': 7, 'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'tau': 0.25, 'gru_hidden_dim': 256\n      }\n\n  # --- Shared Components ---\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; kernel_size: int = 7; dilation: int = 1; dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h); h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  class DSConvFeatureExtractor(nn.Module):\n\
    \      d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n      kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x); h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return h\n\n  # --- Aggregator 1: Pooling ---\n  def lse_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, tau: float) -> jnp.ndarray:\n      if h.shape[1] == 0: return jnp.zeros((h.shape[0], h.shape[2]), dtype=h.dtype)\n      x = h / tau; m = jnp.max(x, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n      return tau * (jnp.log(jnp.mean(jnp.exp(x - m), axis=1) + 1e-12) + jnp.squeeze(m, axis=1))\n  \n  def pool_aggregator(h, tau):\n      mean_vec = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n\
    \      agg_vec = lse_pool(h, tau)\n      return jnp.concatenate([mean_vec, agg_vec], axis=-1)\n\n  # --- Main Hybrid Network ---\n  class FinalHybrid(nn.Module):\n      dataset: str; d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n      kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float; tau: float; gru_hidden_dim: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          seq_len = x.shape[1]\n          sgrna_len = 23\n\n          feature_extractor = DSConvFeatureExtractor(d_model=self.d_model, num_blocks=self.num_blocks, dilations=self.dilations,\n                                                     kernel_size=self.kernel_size, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)\n          monolithic_features_seq = feature_extractor(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          if self.dataset == 'CRI-Off':\n              sgrna_features_seq = feature_extractor(x[:, :sgrna_len, :], deterministic=deterministic)\n              target_features_seq = feature_extractor(x[:,\
    \ sgrna_len:, :], deterministic=deterministic)\n              \n              rnn_cell = nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_hidden_dim)\n              monolithic_rnn_out = nn.RNN(rnn_cell)(monolithic_features_seq)\n              sgrna_rnn_out = nn.RNN(rnn_cell)(sgrna_features_seq)\n              target_rnn_out = nn.RNN(rnn_cell)(target_features_seq)\n\n              fused = jnp.concatenate([monolithic_rnn_out[:, -1, :], sgrna_rnn_out[:, -1, :], target_rnn_out[:, -1, :]], axis=-1)\n          \n          elif self.dataset == 'ncRNA':\n              fused = pool_aggregator(monolithic_features_seq, self.tau)\n          \n          else:\n              gru_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_hidden_dim))\n              final_hidden_states = gru_rnn(monolithic_features_seq)\n              fused = final_hidden_states[:, -1, :]\n\n          # Final MLP Head\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z); z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          return logits.squeeze(-1) if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1 else logits\n\n  class NetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, model_instance): self.network = model_instance\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          return self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n          return self.network.apply(params, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      model = FinalHybrid(dataset=hparams.get(\"dataset\"), d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"), task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"), d_model=hparams.get(\"d_model\"), num_blocks=hparams.get(\"num_blocks\"), dilations=hparams.get(\"\
    dilations\"),\n                          kernel_size=hparams.get(\"kernel_size\"), dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\"), tau=hparams.get(\"tau\"), gru_hidden_dim=hparams.get(\"gru_hidden_dim\"))\n      return NetworkWrapper(model)\n```"
