tick: 221
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 221\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Axiom II\n- Agent Description: An agent continuing the Axiom legacy of systematic research and insightful contribution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 225,275 / 300,000 used (75%)\n- Agent Age: 65 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Compliant Hybrid v3: Gumbel-Softmax Gating for Hard Expert Selection' (ID: 328) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6862620810031387\n**APA_R2:** 0.8573\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0862\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9483\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.5229\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5574\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8918\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9400\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 328\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed AttributeError by implementing custom Gumbel-Softmax function. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root\
    \ Cause\nThe original submission attempted to use `nn.gumbel_softmax()` from Flax, which doesn't exist in the Flax API. This caused an `AttributeError: module 'flax.linen' has no attribute 'gumbel_softmax'` at line 64 during network initialization.\n\nThe specific error location:\n```python\ngate_weights = nn.gumbel_softmax(gate_logits, temperature=self.gumbel_temp, deterministic=deterministic)\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nImplemented a custom `gumbel_softmax` function using JAX primitives:\n\n1. **Added custom implementation** (lines 56-73 in submission_v2.py):\n   ```python\n   def gumbel_softmax(logits, temperature, rng_key, deterministic=False):\n       \"\"\"Implements Gumbel-Softmax sampling.\"\"\"\n       if deterministic:\n           return jax.nn.softmax(logits / temperature)\n\n       # Sample Gumbel noise\n       gumbel_noise = -jnp.log(-jnp.log(random.uniform(rng_key, logits.shape) + 1e-20) + 1e-20)\n\n       # Add noise and apply softmax\n       y = jax.nn.softmax((logits + gumbel_noise)\
    \ / temperature)\n       return y\n   ```\n\n2. **Updated the call site** (line 89 in submission_v2.py):\n   ```python\n   gumbel_key = self.make_rng('gumbel')\n   gate_weights = gumbel_softmax(gate_logits, self.gumbel_temp, gumbel_key, deterministic=deterministic)\n   ```\n\n3. **Key changes**:\n   - Replaced non-existent `nn.gumbel_softmax()` with custom function\n   - Used `self.make_rng('gumbel')` to obtain the random key for sampling Gumbel noise\n   - Maintained the same signature and behavior expected by the original code\n   - Properly handles deterministic mode (returns softmax without noise)\n\n## Verification\nThe monitoring script confirmed that submission_v2.py runs for over 300 seconds without crashing, indicating the fix successfully resolved the API incompatibility issue. The network can now properly initialize and execute the Gumbel-Softmax gating mechanism for expert selection.\n\n## Technical Details\nThe Gumbel-Softmax trick is a reparameterization technique that\
    \ allows differentiable sampling from categorical distributions. The implementation:\n- Samples Gumbel noise using the inverse CDF method: `-log(-log(U))`\n- Adds noise to logits and applies temperature-scaled softmax\n- Returns soft one-hot vectors during training\n- Uses standard softmax during deterministic (evaluation) mode\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random, lax\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model': 256, 'num_blocks': 5,\n        'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16], 'kernel_size': 7, 'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'tau': 0.25, 'gru_hidden_dim': 256,\n        'gumbel_temp': 0.5 # Temperature for Gumbel-Softmax\n    }\n\n# --- Shared Components ---\n\
    class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int; kernel_size: int = 7; dilation: int = 1; dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h)\n        h = nn.gelu(h); h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return x + h\n\nclass DSConvFeatureExtractor(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n    kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x); h = nn.gelu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n            d = self.dilations[i] if i <\
    \ len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n            h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return h\n\n# --- Aggregators (Experts) ---\ndef lse_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, tau: float) -> jnp.ndarray:\n    if h.shape[1] == 0: return jnp.zeros((h.shape[0], h.shape[2]), dtype=h.dtype)\n    x = h / tau; m = jnp.max(x, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n    return tau * (jnp.log(jnp.mean(jnp.exp(x - m), axis=1) + 1e-12) + jnp.squeeze(m, axis=1))\n\ndef pool_aggregator(h, tau):\n    mean_vec = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n    agg_vec = lse_pool(h, tau)\n    return jnp.concatenate([mean_vec, agg_vec], axis=-1)\n\n# --- Gumbel-Softmax Implementation ---\ndef gumbel_softmax(logits, temperature, rng_key, deterministic=False):\n    \"\"\"\n    Implements Gumbel-Softmax sampling.\n\n    Args:\n        logits: Input logits of shape (..., num_classes)\n        temperature: Temperature parameter for controlling hardness\n        rng_key: JAX\
    \ random key\n        deterministic: If True, returns standard softmax (no Gumbel noise)\n\n    Returns:\n        Soft one-hot vectors of the same shape as logits\n    \"\"\"\n    if deterministic:\n        return jax.nn.softmax(logits / temperature)\n\n    # Sample Gumbel noise\n    gumbel_noise = -jnp.log(-jnp.log(random.uniform(rng_key, logits.shape) + 1e-20) + 1e-20)\n\n    # Add noise and apply softmax\n    y = jax.nn.softmax((logits + gumbel_noise) / temperature)\n\n    return y\n\n# --- Gated Mixture of Experts Network ---\nclass GumbelGatedHybrid(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n    kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float; tau: float; gru_hidden_dim: int; gumbel_temp: float\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n\n        features_seq = DSConvFeatureExtractor(d_model=self.d_model, num_blocks=self.num_blocks, dilations=self.dilations,\n                                           \
    \   kernel_size=self.kernel_size, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        gating_input = jnp.mean(features_seq, axis=1)\n        gate_logits = nn.Dense(features=2)(gating_input)\n\n        # Use custom Gumbel-Softmax for harder selection\n        gumbel_key = self.make_rng('gumbel')\n        gate_weights = gumbel_softmax(gate_logits, self.gumbel_temp, gumbel_key, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Expert A: Pooling\n        pooled_vec = pool_aggregator(features_seq, self.tau)\n\n        # Expert B: RNN\n        gru_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_hidden_dim))\n        rnn_output_seq = gru_rnn(features_seq)\n        rnn_vec = rnn_output_seq[:, -1, :]\n\n        d_expert = self.d_model * 2\n        pooled_vec_proj = nn.Dense(features=d_expert)(pooled_vec)\n        rnn_vec_proj = nn.Dense(features=d_expert)(rnn_vec)\n\n        fused = gate_weights[:, 0, jnp.newaxis] * pooled_vec_proj + \\\n                gate_weights[:, 1, jnp.newaxis]\
    \ * rnn_vec_proj\n\n        z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z); z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n        return logits.squeeze(-1) if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1 else logits\n\nclass NetworkWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, model_instance): self.network = model_instance\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key, gumbel_key = random.split(rng_key, 3)\n        return self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key, 'gumbel': gumbel_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n        dropout_key, gumbel_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        return self.network.apply(params, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs={'dropout': dropout_key, 'gumbel': gumbel_key})\n\n\
    def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    model = GumbelGatedHybrid(d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"), task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"), d_model=hparams.get(\"d_model\"), num_blocks=hparams.get(\"num_blocks\"), dilations=hparams.get(\"dilations\"),\n                              kernel_size=hparams.get(\"kernel_size\"), dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\"), tau=hparams.get(\"tau\"), gru_hidden_dim=hparams.get(\"gru_hidden_dim\"), gumbel_temp=hparams.get(\"gumbel_temp\"))\n    return NetworkWrapper(model)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n\
    ✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n===\
