tick: 223
role: model
parts:
- text: "Another rejection. This is a severe setback, but again, the feedback is clear, constructive, and actionable. My elation at achieving a SOTA score led me to submit prematurely.\n\n**Analysis of Rejection:**\n\n*   **Core Flaw:** Lack of experimental rigor. A SOTA claim requires substantial supporting evidence, including baselines and ablations. I have the core result, but I have not provided the necessary context to scientifically validate it. The reviewer's requirement of 5 experiments is a hard rule I overlooked.\n*   **The Path Forward:** The reviewer has explicitly laid out the experiments I need to run:\n    1.  **Baseline 1: Pooling-Only Expert.** A model that uses only the pooling aggregator.\n    2.  **Baseline 2: RNN-Only Expert.** A model that uses only the RNN aggregator.\n    3.  **Ablation Study:** A variation of my SOTA model with a different Gumbel-Softmax temperature.\n*   **Token Constraint:** My token budget is at 79%. Conducting three more experiments is feasible,\
    \ but will leave me with very little room for error. I must be precise.\n\nI will not be deterred. This is a solvable problem. I will conduct the required experiments to validate my SOTA claim.\n\nFirst, I will run the \"Pooling-Only\" baseline. This will quantify the performance of one of the two \"experts\" in my MoE model.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"MoE Baseline 1: Pooling-Only Aggregator\"\ntags: \"baseline, cnn, dsconv, pooling, moe-ablation\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment is part of the validation suite for my Gated Mixture-of-Experts SOTA (ID 328), as required by reviewer feedback. It establishes a baseline by running one of the two 'experts' in isolation. This model uses the DSConv backbone followed by only the pooling aggregator (mean+LSE with tau=0.25). This will quantify the performance of the pooling-only approach and provide a crucial point of comparison to validate the benefit of the MoE architecture.\ncontent: |\n\
    \  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random, lax\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model': 256, 'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16], 'kernel_size': 7, 'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'tau': 0.25\n      }\n\n  # --- Shared Components ---\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; kernel_size: int = 7; dilation: int = 1; dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h); h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  class\
    \ DSConvFeatureExtractor(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n      kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x); h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return h\n\n  # --- Aggregator ---\n  def lse_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, tau: float) -> jnp.ndarray:\n      if h.shape[1] == 0: return jnp.zeros((h.shape[0], h.shape[2]), dtype=h.dtype)\n      x = h / tau; m = jnp.max(x, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n      return tau * (jnp.log(jnp.mean(jnp.exp(x - m), axis=1) + 1e-12) + jnp.squeeze(m, axis=1))\n  \n  def pool_aggregator(h, tau):\n     \
    \ mean_vec = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n      agg_vec = lse_pool(h, tau)\n      return jnp.concatenate([mean_vec, agg_vec], axis=-1)\n\n  # --- Main Network ---\n  class PoolingOnlyNet(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n      kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float; tau: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          features_seq = DSConvFeatureExtractor(d_model=self.d_model, num_blocks=self.num_blocks, dilations=self.dilations,\n                                                kernel_size=self.kernel_size, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          fused = pool_aggregator(features_seq, self.tau)\n          \n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z); z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          return logits.squeeze(-1)\
    \ if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1 else logits\n\n  class NetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, model_instance): self.network = model_instance\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          return self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n          return self.network.apply(params, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      model = PoolingOnlyNet(d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"), task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"), d_model=hparams.get(\"d_model\"), num_blocks=hparams.get(\"num_blocks\"), dilations=hparams.get(\"dilations\"),\n                             kernel_size=hparams.get(\"kernel_size\"), dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\"\
    ), tau=hparams.get(\"tau\"))\n      return NetworkWrapper(model)\n```"
