tick: 225
role: model
parts:
- text: "My parallel submission strategy is working. I have received the results for my first baseline, the \"Pooling-Only Aggregator\" (ID 337), while the second baseline runs.\n\n**Analysis of MoE Baseline 1 (ID 337)**\n\n*   **Result:** The score is **0.6725**.\n*   **Significance:** This is a strong result in its own right, outperforming many of my earlier experiments. It validates that a simple, SOTA-aligned pooling model is a very effective generalist.\n*   **Context for MoE:** Most importantly, this score is significantly lower than my Gumbel-gated MoE model (ID 328, score 0.6863). This provides the first piece of hard evidence that my Mixture-of-Experts approach provides a substantial benefit over at least one of its constituent parts.\n\nI now have one running experiment (ID 339, RNN-Only) and one final experiment to conduct: the ablation on the Gumbel-Softmax temperature. My token budget is critical (81%). I will submit my final required experiment now to ensure it is queued. Once\
    \ all three are complete, I will have the full suite of results needed to resubmit my paper.\n\nI will now submit the Gumbel temperature ablation study. I will increase the temperature from 0.5 to 1.0, which should make the gate's selections \"softer\" and closer to a standard softmax. This should result in a lower score, thereby demonstrating the importance of the \"harder\" selection.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"MoE Ablation: Gumbel-Softmax Gating with Higher Temperature\"\ntags: \"ablation, cnn, dsconv, rnn, gating, moe, gumbel-softmax\"\nabstract: |\n  This is the final experiment required by reviewer feedback to validate my MoE SOTA (ID 328). It is an ablation study on the Gumbel-Softmax gate temperature. I have increased the temperature from 0.5 to 1.0. It is hypothesized that this 'softer' temperature will lead to less decisive expert selection, resulting in a lower score than the SOTA model. This will demonstrate that the 'hardness' of the gate is a critical\
    \ component of the model's success.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random, lax\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model': 256, 'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16], 'kernel_size': 7, 'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'tau': 0.25, 'gru_hidden_dim': 256,\n          'gumbel_temp': 1.0 # Increased temperature for ablation\n      }\n\n  def gumbel_softmax(logits, temperature, rng_key, deterministic=False):\n      if deterministic:\n          return jax.nn.softmax(logits / temperature)\n      gumbel_noise = -jnp.log(-jnp.log(random.uniform(rng_key, logits.shape) + 1e-20) + 1e-20)\n      y = jax.nn.softmax((logits + gumbel_noise) / temperature)\n      return y\n\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; kernel_size: int = 7; dilation: int = 1; dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n     \
    \ def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h); h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  class DSConvFeatureExtractor(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n      kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x); h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d,\
    \ self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return h\n\n  def lse_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, tau: float) -> jnp.ndarray:\n      if h.shape[1] == 0: return jnp.zeros((h.shape[0], h.shape[2]), dtype=h.dtype)\n      x = h / tau; m = jnp.max(x, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n      return tau * (jnp.log(jnp.mean(jnp.exp(x - m), axis=1) + 1e-12) + jnp.squeeze(m, axis=1))\n  \n  def pool_aggregator(h, tau):\n      mean_vec = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n      agg_vec = lse_pool(h, tau)\n      return jnp.concatenate([mean_vec, agg_vec], axis=-1)\n\n  class GumbelGatedHybrid(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n      kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float; tau: float; gru_hidden_dim: int; gumbel_temp: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          features_seq = DSConvFeatureExtractor(d_model=self.d_model, num_blocks=self.num_blocks, dilations=self.dilations,\n                          \
    \                      kernel_size=self.kernel_size, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          gating_input = jnp.mean(features_seq, axis=1)\n          gate_logits = nn.Dense(features=2)(gating_input)\n          gumbel_key = self.make_rng('gumbel')\n          gate_weights = gumbel_softmax(gate_logits, self.gumbel_temp, gumbel_key, deterministic=deterministic)\n          pooled_vec = pool_aggregator(features_seq, self.tau)\n          gru_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_hidden_dim))\n          rnn_output_seq = gru_rnn(features_seq)\n          rnn_vec = rnn_output_seq[:, -1, :]\n          d_expert = self.d_model * 2\n          pooled_vec_proj = nn.Dense(features=d_expert)(pooled_vec)\n          rnn_vec_proj = nn.Dense(features=d_expert)(rnn_vec)\n          fused = gate_weights[:, 0, jnp.newaxis] * pooled_vec_proj + \\\n                  gate_weights[:, 1, jnp.newaxis] * rnn_vec_proj\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z);\
    \ z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          return logits.squeeze(-1) if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1 else logits\n\n  class NetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, model_instance): self.network = model_instance\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key, gumbel_key = random.split(rng_key, 3)\n          return self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key, 'gumbel': gumbel_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n          dropout_key, gumbel_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          return self.network.apply(params, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs={'dropout': dropout_key, 'gumbel': gumbel_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      model = GumbelGatedHybrid(d_output=hparams.get(\"\
    d_output\"), task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"), d_model=hparams.get(\"d_model\"), num_blocks=hparams.get(\"num_blocks\"), dilations=hparams.get(\"dilations\"),\n                                kernel_size=hparams.get(\"kernel_size\"), dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\"), tau=hparams.get(\"tau\"), gru_hidden_dim=hparams.get(\"gru_hidden_dim\"), gumbel_temp=hparams.get(\"gumbel_temp\"))\n      return NetworkWrapper(model)\n```"
